  "title": "Tennessee's 3rd Congressional District General Election, 2026",
  "office": "U.S. House of Representatives",
  "jurisdiction": "Tennessee's 3rd Congressional District",
  "state": "Tennessee",
  "district": "3rd Congressional District",
  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 general election for Tennessee's 3rd Congressional District will be held on November 3, 2026, following a primary on August 6, 2026. The district was redrawn in May 2026 under a new congressional map passed by the Tennessee legislature, and covers the greater Chattanooga region including Hamilton, Bradley, and Anderson counties among others. Incumbent Republican Chuck Fleischmann, first elected in 2010 and currently serving as Chairman of the Energy and Water Appropriations Subcommittee, is seeking reelection and faces no primary challenger. Two Democrats \u2014 Anna Golladay and Bryan Martin \u2014 will compete in the primary, and five independent candidates are also on the general election ballot, reflecting the newly competitive dynamics of the redrawn district.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "name": "Chuck Fleischmann",
      "party": "Republican Party",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Chuck Fleischmann has represented Tennessee's 3rd Congressional District since January 2011. He is a conservative Republican who serves as Chairman of the Energy and Water Development Appropriations Subcommittee and sits on the House Appropriations Committee, where he oversees funding for national laboratories, nuclear security, and infrastructure projects such as the Chickamauga Lock. Before Congress, he earned a law degree from the University of Tennessee and co-ran a small law practice with his wife in Chattanooga for 24 years.",
