      "summary": "Anna Golladay is a progressive faith leader, small business owner, and Democrat running for Congress in Tennessee's 3rd District. She owns Biased Apparel, a clothing company she founded in 2011, and serves as CEO of Work of Place, a consulting firm helping faith communities leverage their assets for community economic stability. Previously an associate pastor at St. Elmo United Methodist Church and St. Marks Church in Chattanooga, she holds a Master of Theological Studies from Iliff School of Theology and a Master's in Integrated Marketing Communications from West Virginia University.",
